// Stone 39's other half: a text that is not a number
// stops the bare machine before its next word can be
// said. The hosted doors answer such a text with a
// problem 'attempt' can catch; bare metal has no
// 'nothing' to answer with, and stopping is its way
// of refusing. The proof boots this program and
// checks that the first line stands and the last
// never does.
say "Before the reading"
say "Read: " + asnumber("one hundred")
say "After the reading"
